{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1774312767,"nonce":"lFwVQK5dihGBkBcFO4ivRsUHYE4=","message":"**Implementation spec — state field selection system**\n\n## Approach\n1. **StateFieldPath type + tree constant** in `web/src/types/analysis.ts`: dot-separated path strings, recursive `StateFieldNode` type, `STATE_FIELD_TREE` constant with full hierarchy.\n2. **StateFieldTree component** (`web/src/components/analysis/StateFieldTree.tsx`): recursive tree renderer with expand/collapse chevrons, indentation, React Flow Handles on every node (branch and leaf). Each handle ID encodes the full dot-path for wire routing.\n3. **DataSourceNode rewrite**: replace flat port list with `StateFieldTree`. Top-level items always visible; sub-fields revealed on chevron click. Node auto-sizes via dynamic height calc. Collapsed top-level ports still connectable (full subtree). Uses `useUpdateNodeInternals` to notify React Flow of handle changes on expand/collapse.\n4. **AnalysisWire.fieldPath**: optional `StateFieldPath` on `AnalysisWire` and `AnalysisEdgeData`. `connectNodes` extracts field path from handle ID when source is data source. Top-level handle = undefined fieldPath.\n5. **Edge labels**: both edge components render a small muted label showing the field path suffix (e.g. \".net.hidden\") when `fieldPath` is present in edge data.\n\n## Handle ID encoding\nData source handles use the full dot-path as the handle ID (e.g. `states.net.hidden`). The `connectNodes` action checks if `sourceHandle` contains dots — if so, it stores the full path as `fieldPath` and uses the root segment as `sourcePort` for backward compat.","files":null}]}